(version 1)

# Custom DRC rules for the POWER artwork of the CNC-milled vinyl ADC.
#
# Copper is isolation-milled with an 0.8 mm flat end mill, so 0.8 mm is the hard
# floor on any copper-to-copper gap: the tool cannot enter anything narrower, and
# a gap it cannot enter stays shorted. The Default netclass asks for 0.85 mm --
# the `cnc` fabrication profile's number -- leaving every routed track ~0.025 mm
# of copper either side of the cut as margin for runout and registration.
#
# Every footprint here was audited against that floor. Only the stacking bus
# header sits between the tool diameter and the netclass clearance:
#
#   J3   PinHeader_2x08_P2.54mm_Vertical  -> 0.84 mm pad-to-pad  (30 pairs)
#
# That gap is set by the header's own 2.54 mm pin pitch, not by anything we cut,
# and it still clears the tool in a single pass. The rule below relaxes the
# clearance ONLY between two items that both belong to that footprint. The full
# 0.85 mm stays in force between different components and for every track.
#
# Needing no exception: DIP-8/20 LongPads at 0.94 mm, the radial electrolytics
# at 1.90 mm, and every axial passive and disc at 3.4 mm or wider.

(rule "J3_intra_pad_clearance"
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('J3') && B.memberOfFootprint('J3')")
	(constraint clearance (min 0.8mm)))
